	"book_lg_medieval_fort_1": "The Guard's Footprints",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_1_d": "Simin says the fort's last guard left a sign for us. Walk to the marked stone pillar near the fort and stand beside it.",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_1_s": "A scrap of red cloth with the fort's crest is caught under the pillar. The guard was in a hurry and avoided the main road; his tracks lead away from the fort.",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_2": "The Forgotten Well",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_2_d": "Pouria tells of an old well outside the fort where the guard drew water. The next pillar stands beside it.",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_2_s": "A fresh knot ties a rope beside the well. Someone used it only days ago, and something glints at the bottom that you cannot reach yet.",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_3": "The Bell Cave",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_3_d": "Arash says a bell rings from a stone cave east of the fort. Walk in through its doorway and stand beside the pillar in the middle.",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_3_s": "Inside the cave it is cool and dark, and the bell rings from right here. The guard hid it so that only friends would hear it when danger came near.",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_4": "The Broken Bridge",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_4_d": "Bahram says the guard crossed the farmland and left something by a broken bridge. Reach the fourth pillar.",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_4_s": "Under the broken bridge, in a crack in the stone, lies a half-burnt note: Take the seal to Simin and trust no one else.",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_5": "Simin's Treasure",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_5_d": "The last pillar completes the tale: the king's seal is guarded here. Reach it to finish the legend of the fort.",
	"book_lg_medieval_fort_5_s": "The hall is silent and the king's seal gleams on its plinth. Now you know why the guard left: he did not steal the seal, he kept it so the fort would not be forgotten.",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_1": "The White Wolf's Trail",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_1_d": "Bahman speaks of a white wolf's tracks in the snow. Follow the trail to the first stone pillar.",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_1_s": "Under the snow you find an empty wolf den. The hunter says the wolves left when an unnatural cold arrived; something from the far north drove them out.",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_2": "The Abandoned Cabin",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_2_d": "Shirin says a hunter stayed long ago in a far cabin. The second pillar is there.",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_2_s": "Beside a fire that gives no smoke lies a frozen travel journal. The innkeeper says its owner had seen a light on the far side of the lake.",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_3": "The Unfrozen Spring",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_3_d": "Bahman says there is a spring that never freezes, even in winter. The third pillar stands beside it.",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_3_s": "Cracks on the frozen lake all meet at one point. A dark shape lies under the ice, but it is not yet time to bring it out.",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_4": "The Peak of Stars",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_4_d": "Darab says the stars hang low over one peak at night. Reach the last pillar.",
	"book_lg_frozen_north_4_s": "Tall stones stand in a ring and it is warm in the middle. The elder says this is the heart of winter; as long as no one wakes it, the north stays alive.",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_1": "The First Caravan's Well",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_1_d": "Kaveh says the first caravan drew water at a nameless well. The first stone pillar is there.",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_1_s": "A lost caravan's trail is still in the sand; the camels were mid-stride when the storm hit. The signs say everyone was alive.",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_2": "The Red Pillar",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_2_d": "Golnar tells of a red stone travellers used to find their way. Find the second pillar.",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_2_s": "Beside a dry well you find a sealed jar. The innkeeper says this well's water only returns at night.",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_3": "The Sand Inscription",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_3_d": "Mehrdad says the wind uncovered an old inscription. The third pillar stands beside it.",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_3_s": "An old forge lies half-buried in the sand. From the iron scraps the smith says it once made horseshoes and tools for the caravan.",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_4": "The Desert Star",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_4_d": "Kaveh says the last mark is where caravans gathered under the stars. Reach the last pillar.",
	"book_lg_desert_caravan_4_s": "In the shade of a great rock, the caravan's map is carved on hide, and its last mark leads to a hidden oasis; the caravan was not lost, it was hiding.",
	"scen_space_colony": "Space Colony",
	"scen_space_colony_desc": "The Moon: grey dust, crystal spires, a black sky, a landing pad with a rocket, a habitat dome and a lab.\nTry: harvest crystals for wood, build domes and gardens from glass, set up solar panels and grow your base.",
	"book_dust_walker": "Moonwalk",
	"book_dust_walker_d": "Walk on the grey lunar dust.",
	"book_crystal_find": "Crystal Field",
	"book_crystal_find_d": "Find a field of crystal spires.",
	"book_crater_rim": "Crater Rim",
	"book_crater_rim_d": "Climb the high lunar cliffs (18 m).",
	"book_dome_builder": "Dome Builder",
	"book_dome_builder_d": "Place 30 glass blocks.",
	"book_lg_space_colony_1": "Landing Mark",
	"book_lg_space_colony_1_d": "Sara says the first lander left a marker beside a distant crater. The first pillar is there.",
	"book_lg_space_colony_1_s": "An old astronaut's footprints still lie in the dust; there is no wind to erase them.",
	"book_lg_space_colony_2": "The Silent Station",
	"book_lg_space_colony_2_d": "Nima speaks of an abandoned station whose receiver still repeats one message. Find the second pillar.",
	"book_lg_space_colony_2_s": "The station is silent, yet a small light glows on its control panel. Nima says someone left it on before leaving.",
	"book_lg_space_colony_3": "Crystal Garden",
	"book_lg_space_colony_3_d": "Kamran says the crystals glow in the dark. The third pillar stands among them.",
	"book_lg_space_colony_3_s": "The crystal spires look like a glass forest bending the starlight; Kamran wonders if they are seeds too.",
	"book_lg_space_colony_4": "End of the Message",
	"book_lg_space_colony_4_d": "Ayda says the message comes from farther away. Reach the last pillar.",
	"book_lg_space_colony_4_s": "On a flat stone in the middle of the plain, visible only at night: \"Build a home here.\" The message was just as simple.",
	"book_legend": "🧭 Next legend stop: %s — about %s m, %s",
	"book_lg_green_valley_1": "The First Farmer's Stone",
	"book_lg_green_valley_1_d": "Ali says the valley's first farmer set a stone to mark the land. Reach the first stone pillar.",
	"book_lg_green_valley_1_s": "An old rusty plough lies by the ancient tree. The farmer says his grandfather planted the valley's first wheat right here.",
	"book_lg_green_valley_2": "The Bread Spring",
	"book_lg_green_valley_2_d": "Maryam tells of a spring whose water the old bakers used for their dough. The second pillar is beside it.",
	"book_lg_green_valley_2_s": "The ruined mill still smells of flour. The baker says that long ago the whole valley baked its bread from this place.",
	"book_lg_green_valley_3": "Kite Hill",
	"book_lg_green_valley_3_d": "Reza tells of a hill where children flew kites. The third pillar is there.",
	"book_lg_green_valley_3_s": "From the hilltop the valley looks like a green bowl split by a river. The guide says the elders drew their water map from here.",
	"book_lg_green_valley_4": "The Valley's Treasure",
	"book_lg_green_valley_4_d": "The last pillar marks where farmers hid the best harvest of the year. Reach it.",
	"book_lg_green_valley_4_s": "Under the last tree stands a stone carved with family names. The valley belonged to no one; everyone built it together, and now you add your own name.",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_1": "The Bottle on the Shore",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_1_d": "Ali says a captain left a bottle with a map on the shore. Reach the first pillar.",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_1_s": "In the sand you find a piece of a ship's mast and the ashes of an old fire. Someone was stranded here before you.",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_2": "The Shell Cave",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_2_d": "Reza says a small cave holds glittering shells. The second pillar is there.",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_2_s": "Tally marks for counting days are cut into the rock; the last one is unfinished. The guide says castaways kept their hope here.",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_3": "The Lookout Fire",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_3_d": "Maryam says islanders once lit a fire to guide ships. The third pillar is there.",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_3_s": "In a small cave by the shore are dried bread and a few water skins. The baker says someone stored them for whoever came next.",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_4": "The Lonely Captain's Treasure",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_4_d": "The last pillar is where the captain hid his treasure. Reach it.",
	"book_lg_island_castaway_4_s": "A signal fire stands on the island's highest point. Light it, and any ship that comes one day will know someone is here.",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_1": "The Old Ledger",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_1_d": "Maryam says a merchant hid his ledger under a stone pillar. Reach the first pillar.",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_1_s": "A brass scale lies in the old market. The baker says the old merchant always weighed honestly, which is why the city trusted him.",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_2": "The Night Market",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_2_d": "Reza tells of an old market lit up at night. The second pillar is beside it.",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_2_s": "A dusty ledger lies in the caravanserai; on its last page a debt is written, then crossed out.",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_3": "The Forgotten Warehouse",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_3_d": "Ali says there is an old warehouse outside the city. The third pillar is there.",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_3_s": "By the granary the farmer says the merchant sold grain at half price during the famine and never told a soul.",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_4": "The Merchants' Vault",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_4_d": "The last pillar is where the merchants hid their wealth. Reach it.",
	"book_lg_merchant_city_4_s": "In the trade hall a golden coin sits under glass. The baker says the city's wealth is not the coin; it is the people's trust.",
